# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
C('kind', "one adult in plain clothes and one small child stand whole-figure, side view, in front of a plain school gate with a flat pavement line, same distance from the viewer, a plain wall behind. Only whether the adult comes to fetch the child or leaves the child at the gate changes.",
  "'s Ochtends breng ik mijn zoon weg en 's middags haal ik hem op.", "In the morning I drop my son off and in the afternoon I pick him up.")
K('ophalen', "One drawing, one panel. A small child stands inside the open school gate with a schoolbag on its back and one hand stretched up, and an adult stands outside on the pavement holding out a hand to take it. The child's schoolbag is on, the gate is open.",
  "a child's raised hand meeting the adult's hand at the open gate.",
  "the adult walking away while the child goes in through the gate (wegbrengen); an adult carrying a box (optillen); an adult waving goodbye to a bus (not the card); a child running alone (not the card).",
  "Pair with wegbrengen. The only difference is the direction: the adult reaches in to collect the child here, and leaves the child inside there.",
  "haal ... op", "Ik haal mijn zoon van school op.", "I pick up my son from school.", "heeft opgehaald",
  "Een kind met een schooltas staat bij een open hek en een volwassene aan de andere kant pakt zijn hand.")
K('wegbrengen', "One drawing, one panel. A small child with a schoolbag walks in through the open school gate looking back, and an adult stands on the pavement outside with a raised waving hand and one foot turned away from the gate. The adult's hands are empty.",
  "an adult's waving hand outside the gate as a child walks in.",
  "the adult holding the child's hand inside the gate (ophalen); a child riding on an adult's shoulders (not the card); an adult pushing a pram (not the card); a child at a desk in class (not the card).",
  "Pair with ophalen. The only difference is the direction: the adult leaves the child inside and walks off here, and takes the child's hand there.",
  "breng ... weg", "'s Ochtends breng ik hem weg.", "In the morning I take him there.", "heeft weggebracht",
  "Een kind met een schooltas loopt door een open hek en een volwassene aan de straatkant zwaait.")

C('pakket', "one plain parcel wrapped in simple paper and string, a plain counter with a flat top seen from the front, one adult in plain clothes on the customer side, same distance from the viewer, a plain wall behind. Only whether the adult hands the parcel in or takes it away changes.",
  "Ik stuur het pakket op en mijn buurman haalt zijn pakket af.", "I send the parcel off and my neighbour collects his parcel.")
K('opsturen', "One drawing, one panel. An adult at the customer side of a counter pushes a plain wrapped parcel across the top with both hands flat on it, the clerk's empty hand waiting on the far side, a small arrow showing the parcel moving away from the adult.",
  "both hands pushing a parcel across the counter away from the adult.",
  "the adult taking the parcel from the clerk's hands (afhalen); an adult dropping a letter in a postbox (not the card); an adult carrying a parcel up the stairs (not the card); an adult handing a gift to a friend (aanbieden).",
  "Pair with afhalen. The only difference is the direction: the parcel moves away from the adult here, towards the adult there.",
  "stuur ... op", "Ik stuur het pakket op.", "I send off the parcel.", "heeft opgestuurd",
  "Een volwassene schuift een pakje over een balie naar een medewerker toe.")
K('afhalen', "One drawing, one panel. An adult stands at the customer side of the same counter and pulls a plain wrapped parcel towards their chest with both hands, the clerk's hands letting go of the far side, a small arrow showing the parcel moving toward the adult.",
  "both hands drawing a parcel across the counter towards the adult.",
  "the adult pushing the parcel across to the clerk (opsturen); an adult carrying a parcel through a front door (meenemen); an adult picking up a child at a gate (ophalen); an adult receiving a gift from a friend (aannemen).",
  "Pair with opsturen. The only difference is the direction: the parcel moves towards the adult here, away from the adult there.",
  "haal ... af", "Ik haal het pakket af.", "I collect the parcel.", "heeft afgehaald",
  "Een volwassene trekt met twee handen een pakje over een balie naar zich toe.")

C('bord', "one plain round plate seen from above on a plain table, a fork and a knife beside it, one adult's hand and arm entering from the lower edge, same plate size on the page. Only how much food is on the plate changes.",
  "Ik eet alles op, maar mijn broer laat wat groente over.", "I eat everything up, but my brother leaves some vegetables.")
K('opeten', "One drawing, one panel. A plain round plate seen from above is completely empty and clean apart from a fork laid across it, with a few small crumb dots at the edge. An adult's hand rests on the table beside the plate.",
  "a completely empty plate with a fork laid across it.",
  "the same plate with a heap of food left on it (overlaten); a plate that has not been touched (not the card); an adult drinking from a glass (not the card); an adult washing the plate (afwassen).",
  "Pair with overlaten. The only difference is the plate: bare and empty here, with a pile of food left on one side there.",
  "eet ... op", "Ik eet alles op.", "I eat everything up.", "heeft opgegeten",
  "Een leeg bord ligt van boven gezien op een tafel en er ligt een vork schuin op het bord.")
K('overlaten', "One drawing, one panel. The same plain round plate seen from above has a heap of three round vegetables and a small pile of rice pushed to one side, the other half of the plate empty, and the fork lying beside it. An adult's hand rests next to the plate.",
  "a plate half empty with a heap of food pushed to one side.",
  "the same plate completely empty (opeten); a plate heaped full and untouched (not the card); food being thrown into a bin (weggooien); a plate being passed to another person (doorgeven).",
  "Pair with opeten. The only difference is the plate: a heap of food left on one side here, nothing left there.",
  "laat ... over", "Ik laat wat groente over.", "I leave some vegetables.", "heeft overgelaten",
  "Een bord van boven gezien heeft een hoopje groente en rijst aan één kant en de andere helft is leeg.")

C('afwas', "one plain kitchen sink seen from the front, a plain tap above it, a plate rack beside it, a stack of three plain plates, one adult in plain clothes standing at the sink, same distance from the viewer. Only whether the plate is in wet hands under soap or in a cloth changes.",
  "Ik was de borden af en mijn zus droogt ze af.", "I wash the plates and my sister dries them.")
K('afwassen', "One drawing, one panel. An adult stands at the sink with both hands in a basin of water topped with a few soap bubbles and holds one wet plate; a small stack of three dirty plates waits beside the basin and the plate rack is empty.",
  "a plate in soapy water with bubbles beside a stack of three plates.",
  "an adult rubbing a plate with a dry cloth beside a full rack (afdrogen); an adult scrubbing a floor with a cloth (schoonmaken); an adult filling a glass at the tap (not the card); an adult carrying a stack of plates to a table (not the card).",
  "Pair with afdrogen. The only difference is the water: soapy hands in a basin here, a dry cloth and a full rack there.",
  "was ... af", "Ik was elke avond af.", "I wash up every evening.", "heeft afgewassen",
  "Een volwassene staat met beide handen in een bak water met zeepbellen en heeft een nat bord in de hand.")
K('afdrogen', "One drawing, one panel. An adult stands at the same sink and rubs one plate with a plain cloth held in both hands, a plate rack beside it already holding two plates, and the basin pushed aside empty and flat. Three short shine lines mark the plate.",
  "a cloth rubbing a plate beside a rack holding clean plates.",
  "hands in soapy water with bubbles (afwassen); an adult wiping a table with a cloth (schoonmaken); an adult drying hair with a towel (not the card); an adult hanging a cloth on a hook (not the card).",
  "Pair with afwassen. The only difference is the water: none, a dry cloth and a stocked rack here, soapy water with bubbles there.",
  "droog ... af", "Ik droog de borden af.", "I dry the plates.", "heeft afgedroogd",
  "Een volwassene wrijft een bord met een doek en in het rek staan al twee borden.")

C('cadeau', "one adult in plain clothes and one friend stand whole-figure, side view, facing each other at a plain table, a small plain wrapped present with a ribbon, same distance from the viewer, a plain wall behind. Only whether the present is held out or is being taken changes.",
  "Ik bied mijn vriend een cadeau aan en hij neemt het aan.", "I offer my friend a present and he accepts it.")
K('aanbieden', "One drawing, one panel. An adult stands facing a friend and holds a small wrapped present with a ribbon out on two flat hands at chest height, arms stretched, the present between them, the friend's hands still down at the sides.",
  "a present held out on two flat hands, the friend's hands still down.",
  "the friend's hands closing round the present (aannemen); an adult handing a parcel across a counter (opsturen); an adult passing a loaf along a table (doorgeven); an adult tucking the present in a bag (not the card).",
  "Pair with aannemen. The only difference is the friend's hands: still down by the sides here, closing round the present there.",
  "bied ... aan", "Ik bied mijn vriend een cadeau aan.", "I offer my friend a present.", "heeft aangeboden",
  "Een volwassene houdt een ingepakt cadeautje met een lint naar voren op twee vlakke handen.")
K('aannemen', "One drawing, one panel. A friend stands facing an adult and closes both hands round a small wrapped present with a ribbon, the adult's flat hands still beneath it, the friend's arms bent towards the chest and the face smiling.",
  "two hands closing round the present, arms bent in.",
  "the adult holding the present out with flat hands (aanbieden); a friend pushing the present back (not the card); a friend grabbing a rope (vasthouden); a friend picking a parcel off a counter (afhalen).",
  "Pair with aanbieden. The only difference is the friend's hands: closed round the present here, held down by the sides there.",
  "neem ... aan", "Ik neem het cadeau aan.", "I accept the present.", "heeft aangenomen",
  "Een vriend sluit beide handen om een ingepakt cadeautje en trekt het naar zich toe.")
